matosdev","id":199598874,"node_id":"U_kgDOC-WjGg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199598874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev","html_url":"https://github.com/joaomatosdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joaomatosdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T10:03:01Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T10:05:34Z","body":"> In that case you need to use `quarkus.management.enable-compression`\n\nI hadn't seen that config before. Thanks for that 👍 \n\nHowever, after that, I tested with the following configuration in `application.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nmanagement:\n  enabled: true\n  port: 8081\n  root-path: /\n  enable-compression: true\n```\nRequest:\n```bash\ncurl -i -H \"Accept-Encoding: gzip\" http://localhost:8081/metrics \n\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nContent-Type: application/openmetrics-text; version=1.0.0; charset=utf-8\ncontent-length: 18471\n```\n\nDespite the Accept-Encoding: gzip header being present, the response is still not compressed. I also checked various media type responses on management, and none return the output compressed.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/quarkusio/quarkus/issues/comments/3297334838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perfo